From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] layer: late input sampling

A game that reads its input right after vkQueuePresentKHR returns still
reads it a whole frame before it needs to with the FIFO queue bounded:
a light game renders in a few milliseconds and then waits for the next
latch. With GAMESCOPE_WSI_LATE_SAMPLING=1 the layer holds such a game
until it has just enough time left to make the next latch.

gamescope's present_timing reports carry, for each frame, when its
rendering finished and the vblank that shows it. The report itself, and
its latch time, come when gamescope takes the commit as done, which for
FIFO can be most of a refresh before the latch that shows it, so the
pacing works from the vblank. The layer keeps the time from releasing
the app to the frame being ready over the last 128 frames. While the
slowest of them, a margin (GAMESCOPE_WSI_LATE_SAMPLING_MARGIN, default
2000 us) and gamescope's latch lead (3 ms) fit in one frame interval, a
present waits for its own report and then sleeps until the next frame's
vblank minus all three. When they no longer fit, presents keep the FIFO
queue bound, so a heavy game loses no frames. A paced frame shown more
than 1.5 intervals after the previous one missed: the margin grows
1.5 ms and decays 1 us per frame on time, and 4 misses within 10 s stop
the pacing for 10 s.

Needs 0054.

